# Jak 1: the stick beside a resting menu pointer (a player's report, 2026-11-16: "load game is new game ... only jak 1";
# the owner: "they may be confusing it with the input just clicking something else by accident"). Start opens the
# title menu; the right hand points up into it (the dot on a row near the top) and shakes a little, as a hand held
# still on a headset does (0.3 degrees, every 4 frames); the left stick down twice moves the highlight two rows; then
# A. Expect the highlight to stay where the stick put it (p-stick, p-stick-held) and A to pick that row (p-after): to
# 0.1.1 the shake counted as a move of the dot, which chose its row back from the stick. Run with
# JAKVR_POINTER_TRACE=1.
